WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.440
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:08.800
Let's now go to some stunning new polling
data which reveals that there could be a brutal

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.900
2024 election cycle coming for Republicans.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.060
And it is all revealed thanks to a Fox News
poll.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:21.859
Now, I want to remind people there's no hypocrisy
in saying Fox News content is agit trash that

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:23.810
should be flushed down the toilet.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.189
But we can look at their polling.

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:27.359
Fox news polling is fine.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:30.890
It's relatively well rated and it's generally
pretty well done.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:34.820
You know, Fox doesn't do the polling itself,
just like CNN doesn't do its its own.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.300
They hire a polling firm.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.730
Okay, Check this out.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.160
And this could really be a preview of what's
coming up.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:46.829
Fox poll shows Republicans in for a brutal
2024 election.

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:54.890
Even Fox is admitting on air that the policies
it pushes aren't all that popular with voters.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:01:00.719
They put up a poll and good for them for doing
it, showing how popular certain proposals

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:03.710
to try to mitigate gun violence are with the
American people.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:07.580
And these are not shocking numbers to my audience
because we've been looking at similar polling

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.960
data for more than a decade since the Sandy
Hook shooting in Connecticut.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.740
Background checks for guns, 87% of Americans
favor that.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:23.600
And again, that means in all cases, even interpersonal
sales, all transactions must have a background

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.080
check, enforce existing gun laws, 81%.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.640
You've got to be 21 to buy all guns.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:36.659
That's not the law in a lot of places right
now, 81% ban assault weapons, 80% favor that,

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:41.530
and only 45% believe that more citizens should
be carrying guns.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:48.689
This is yet another issue on which the right
wing media narrative has lost.

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:53.860
The average American Now, obviously, you go
to rural northern Indiana, where I've spent

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.100
some time and you ask people about these things,
very few people will want background checks

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.560
for guns and they'll mostly be against abortion.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.950
Now, that's the other question that this poll
looked at.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:07.880
Abortion should be 56% say legal and 43% say
illegal.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.030
Now when you ask the question.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.100
This way.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.000
This is the split 56 to 43.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.330
If you actually delve further into this and
you explain to people, 99% of abortions happened

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.250
before, I think it's 21 weeks.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.690
And you explain more about the reality of
abortion.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.360
You actually get even more support for abortion.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.420
Just should just flat out be legal before
21 weeks.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.200
And yet there are states that have passed
abortion bans far earlier than that.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.989
So there's a few different things here that
I think are important to consider.

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:46.040
This isn't really newsworthy in the sense
that on policy, Republicans have been losing

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.500
for a long time.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:57.080
In 2016, Trump eked out Hillary and it came
down to under 100,000 votes in three states.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:03.300
But then, as the country continued to move
more to the left, it actually hurt Republicans

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.330
in election.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.360
The 2018 midterms were not great for Republicans.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.780
In 2020, they lost even more, including the
White House.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.799
In 2022, it was going to be a red wave, and
yet the Democratic majority in the Senate

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:17.799
actually grew.

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:22.030
It's interesting to have a red wave where
Democrats gain seats in the Senate, although

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:26.370
they did lose the House and this all may be
culminating in 2024.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:31.159
Now, I'm going to be doing some interesting
podcast appearances coming up.

00:03:31.159 --> 00:03:38.060
And one of the things that I hope comes up
is what's at stake in 2024, because we have

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:42.420
another third of the Senate up for reelection,
as we do every two years.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.720
That's always the case.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:48.340
We have a presidential election, which may
well be a rematch between Joe Biden and Donald

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.340
Trump.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:55.420
And we will have what I believe will be an
inflection point, a fork in the road, whatever

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.879
metaphor you want to use when it comes to
MAGA Trumpism.

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:05.209
MAGA Trumpism has hurt Republicans dramatically,
but it has hung on thanks to the likes of

00:04:05.209 --> 00:04:08.990
Lauren Boebert, Marjorie Taylor GREENE and
